llion but trails badly in cash on hand, plus Libertarian and Green nominees on the ballot. National Republicans have invested in the race, with JD Vance campaigning in the district, though party committees recently pulled money from a neighboring Texas contest.\n\nMost expert raters place the race at Lean Democratic, with two calling it a Tossup, and prediction markets price Gonzalez's chances in the low 80s. Public polling is sparse and dated, with the only usable survey from August showing a narrow 3-point Democratic lead. The combination of a favorable incumbent, a fundraising edge, and market pricing supports a modest Democratic advantage, but the redrawn lines and thin polling leave meaningful room for a Republican upset.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7969, "margin": 4.84}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7826, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7895, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8125, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7373, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7369, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.7694, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7877, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.7446, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.8106, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.7774, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7834, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7562, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.7186, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.7472, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.7411, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.7622, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.7079, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.7312, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.7593, "margin": 5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7567, "margin": 4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.7577, "margin": 4.5}, {"date": "2026-1